## Step walkthrough tours

Each wizard stage shows a **mandatory** spotlight tour the first time the user
sees that stage on desktop (`lg+`). Below `lg` the tour never runs: the only
viewport gate is `shouldRunStepTour` in `StepTour`. Browser `localStorage` key
`roth:step-tour-seen`. No Skip: the user must click through to Got it. Escape
is swallowed while the tour is active. PlanModal itself is not modified;
Household targets local refs, and the footer Next button is resolved via
`findPlanModalPrimaryAction`.

| Stage | Tour id | Status |
| ---- | ---- | ---- |
| Household | `household` | Implemented (filing + state beside field; people; Next) |
| Accounts | `accounts` | Implemented (one tip; spotlights all 3 add buttons) |
| Income | `income` | Implemented (Add income source) |
| Real estate | `realEstate` | Implemented (Add property) |
| Expenses | `expenses` | Implemented (Add expense) |
| Conversion | `conversion` | Empty-state notice; 6-tip year-editor tour only when convertible > 0 |
| After first plan | `strategyPanel` | Left-sidebar Conversion strategy menu; waits until plan / name / auth modals are closed |

## Start gates (`CalculatorHome`)

All must hold before `openFirstRun`:

- mounted, not impersonating, not waiting on profile name
- scenario `loaded`
- active plan is **not** a sample (`!isDefaultPlanId`)
- household is untouched (`isUntouchedHousehold`)
- neither name nor plan modal already open
- auth is `authenticated`, **or** `anonymous` with invite-guest session
  (leftover admin invite link; plan-share invites skip this and open
  create-account)
- After hydrate, a new account with no saved plans gets a blank seed plan,
  which opens first-run.

## Forced vs dismissible

| Signal | Meaning |
| ---- | ---- |
| `nameModal.mode === "firstRun"` | Name modal: no cancel, no backdrop/X close |
| `planModal.mode === "new" && !draftId` | First-plan wizard: no Cancel, no backdrop/X |
| `planModal.mode === "new" && draftId` | Ordinary create: Cancel deletes draft, restores `prevActiveId` |
| `planModal.mode === "edit"` | Edit existing: tabs unlocked, Close commits |

Do not weaken these: first-run must finish (or auth after finish), not escape to
an unnamed blank calculator.

## Wizard behavior (new / first-plan)

- Steps unlock forward only (`unlocked`); edit mode unlocks all tabs.
- Household and Accounts require `isComplete` in new mode; conversion must not
  be empty to finish. Leaving a step (Next / Back / tab) bumps a visit key so
  open entity-card edits remount closed when you return. Enter in a text or
  number field on an open card is the same as Done (selects keep native Enter).
- Last step primary CTA is "Create plan" → `finishPlanModal`.
- `forceCloseModals` clears leftover wizard/auth UI once auth flips to
  authenticated (see `CalculatorHome`).

## Gotchas

- First-run **renames** the existing blank plan; it does not call `newConfig`.
  Ordinary "new" creates a draft id used for cancel/restore.
- `isUntouchedHousehold` is stricter than "no accounts": any filled person
  name / birth / retirement year, or any accounts/income/RE/expenses, skips
  auto first-run. Finished plans that omit accounts must not re-trigger.
- Invite guests can complete the wizard before auth; `finishPlanModal` prefers
  invite-code → create-account over a bare login prompt. Plan-share invite
  links skip the guest wizard and open create-account so the share attaches
  to the new account.
- Profile-name modal takes priority over first-run; do not open the wizard
  underneath it.
- StepTour spotlights must stay in CSS/`position: fixed` space (box-shadow for
  one target; clip-path only for multi-hole tips), not an SVG mask: SVG user
  units drift from `getBoundingClientRect` when browser zoom is not Cmd+0 /
  100%. Remeasure on `visualViewport` resize/scroll as well as window
  resize/scroll.
- First open at a non-default browser zoom looked wrong, but zooming *while*
  the tip was open looked fine: the plan modal enter animation
  (`transform: scale`) skews `getBoundingClientRect`, and body-portaled fixed
  overlays used those mid-animation coords. Remeasure after `MODAL_ENTER_MS`,
  on `animationend`, and via `ResizeObserver` on the targets.
- Household filing/state tips use `right-center` (flip under when the viewport
  is too narrow). `bottom-left` on those small fields looks fine at 100% zoom
  but reads as a floating card over People when the plan modal is tall
  (zoomed out / `min-h-[55vh]`).
- The Roth layout locks zoom in the viewport meta (`maximumScale: 1`,
  `userScalable: false`) so the tool does not pinch-zoom. Form controls are
  still 16px on touch devices so iOS does not auto-zoom a focused field.
- PlanModal is `align="top"` with `min-h` / `max-h` on the dialog. `90vh` plus
  overlay padding is taller than iOS Safari's visible viewport (toolbar is
  inside `vh`, not `dvh`), so Back / Next sit under the browser chrome.
  The overlay is `100dvh` with padding; the dialog is `max-h-full` so the
  footer stays above that gap. Do not put `max-h-[90vh]` back on the dialog.
- `strategyPanel` lives on the calculator sidebar, not in the wizard. Gate on
  closed plan / name / auth modals, a finished non-sample plan with a visible
  strategy menu, and `household` already marked seen (they started first-plan).
  Do not show it on every existing account. Like every other tour, it is
  skipped below `lg` by `shouldRunStepTour`.
